{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts the given array using the Shell sort algorithm, returning a new sorted array.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Clone the array to avoid modifying the original input\n    cloned_arr = list(arr)\n\n    # Start with a large gap, then reduce the gap\n    gap = n // 2\n    while gap > 0:\n        # Perform insertion sort for elements at current gap\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = cloned_arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift elements greater than temp to the right\n            while j >= gap and cloned_arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                cloned_arr[j] = cloned_arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            cloned_arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return cloned_arr"}
