{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "import collections\n\ndef count_Pairs(numbers, expected):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of possible unordered pairs where both elements are unequal.\n    The 'expected' parameter is unused per design context and function description.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    # Use a frequency map to count occurrences of each number\n    freq_map = collections.Counter(numbers)\n\n    # Iterate through unique numbers in the list\n    unique_numbers = sorted(list(freq_map.keys()))\n\n    # Consider pairs of distinct numbers\n    for i in range(len(unique_numbers)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(unique_numbers)):\n            # If numbers are unequal, we can form pairs by multiplying their frequencies\n            num1 = unique_numbers[i]\n            num2 = unique_numbers[j]\n            count += freq_map[num1] * freq_map[num2]\n            \n    return count"}
