{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\n\ndef rotate_right(lst: List[Any], count: int) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Returns a new list with the rotated elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the effective rotation count, handling cases where count is\n    # larger than the list length or zero.\n    effective_count = count % len(lst)\n\n    # Split the list into two parts: the end part that moves to the front,\n    # and the beginning part that follows it.\n    rotated_part = lst[-effective_count:]\n    remaining_part = lst[:-effective_count]\n\n    return rotated_part + remaining_part"}
