{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "def capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces before capital letters in a string, except for single words starting with a capital.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not any(c.isupper() for c in input_string):\n        return input_string\n\n    upper_positions = [i for i, c in enumerate(input_string) if c.isupper()]\n\n    # If it's a single word starting with a capital, return as is (e.g., \"Python\")\n    if len(upper_positions) == 1 and upper_positions[0] == 0:\n        return input_string\n\n    result = []\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        # Insert space before an uppercase letter if it's not the first character\n        if i > 0 and char.isupper():\n            result.append(' ')\n        result.append(char)\n    return ''.join(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a given range that are divisible by every digit they contain.\n    Excludes numbers containing the digit 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        s_num = str(num)\n        \n        # Skip numbers containing the digit '0' as per FR2.\n        if '0' in s_num:\n            continue\n            \n        is_divisible_by_all = True\n        for char_digit in s_num:\n            digit = int(char_digit)\n            # Check if the number is divisible by each of its digits.\n            if num % digit != 0:\n                is_divisible_by_all = False\n                break\n        \n        if is_divisible_by_all:\n            result.append(num)\n            \n    return result"}
