{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "from typing import Sequence\n\ndef find_min_diff(numbers: Sequence[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in a sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if length < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Sequence must contain at least two elements.\")\n    if len(numbers) != length:\n        raise ValueError(\"Provided length does not match the sequence length.\")\n\n    # Sorts the sequence to enable a linear scan for the minimum difference.\n    sorted_nums = sorted(numbers)\n    min_diff = abs(sorted_nums[1] - sorted_nums[0])\n\n    for i in range(2, length):\n        diff = abs(sorted_nums[i] - sorted_nums[i - 1])\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n\n    return min_diff"}
